Parity unit : page:automations/AutomationActivityFeed   kind=page   web route=(unrouted)
Web source  : web/src/features/automations/pages/AutomationActivityFeed.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) + maui-windows workload — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection +
  records + diagnostics + registration, unit-tested headlessly) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view). The generated
  prompt's idealized "AutomationActivityFeed.xaml + AutomationActivityFeedViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/
  Automations" is mapped onto these real conventions — exactly as the peer presentational section AutomationCard
  (feature-views/AutomationCard/{.Model.cs,.cs}) and the W7 ApiLogsPage precedent already are.
- This unit is a presentational leaf, not a routed page: the web source is a component that takes props
  (history / historyStats / isLoading / liveEvents / connectionState) and renders one GlassPanel; manifest route is
  (unrouted). The native AutomationActivityFeed is therefore a ContentControl whose Model property re-projects and
  re-renders on assignment (no fetching, no ViewModel state holder) — the fetch-driven error / stale / offline
  branches are owned by the parent automations page, exactly as in the web source. Because it is unrouted there is
  no NavigationView / ShellPageFactory entry to add (the conditional "if routed" requirement does not apply); the
  peer AutomationCard is wired the same way.
- Manifest models this unit with no API data sources (renders from navigation params / local state), so the
  generated C# client (ADR-004) is not consulted; all branch selection, number/date formatting and label
  resolution happen in the WinUI-free AutomationActivityFeedProjection (web statusConfig / typeMap / timeAgo /
  formatDurationMs / fmtPercent reproduced verbatim, with the web safeNumber() non-finite guard). SI units N/A on
  this surface (no unit-bearing fields); the success rate uses the shared NumberFormatting port (web fmtPercent
  → fmtNumber(_,0)+'%') and the duration the web formatDurationMs tiers.
- All 7 i18n keys already exist verbatim in Strings/en|ar|he/Resources.resw (translation.automations.avgDuration /
  live / noHistory / recentActivity / reconnecting / successRate / totalRuns — 7/7/7 across the three catalogs);
  the surface resolves them through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names (no new catalog rows required).
- a11y: the surface, its glass panel, the connection chip, the stats strip and every live/history row carry an
  AutomationProperties name; decorative glyphs are AccessibilityView.Raw; the loading branch announces via
  LiveRegion. Reduce-motion is honoured by the shared TsFadeIn (web FadeIn delay=0.1). PII-safe diagnostics emit
  only "view.opened slug=AutomationActivityFeed" — never an automation name, error, reason, duration or rate.

=== PARITY ===
PARITY_REQUIRED=11

# Panel (1) — the single web GlassPanel wrapping the whole feed
[x] panel  - GlassPanel1   -> AutomationActivityFeed.cs#Render builds TsGlassPanel{ Padding=24 (web p-6), Content=BuildContent(display) } wrapped in TsFadeIn{ DelayMs=100 } (web FadeIn delay={0.1} <GlassPanel className="p-6">); header + live strip + history compose inside it (BuildContent/BuildHeader/BuildLiveStrip/BuildHistory)

# Data states (3) — loading / empty / success, each a visible region (never blank)
[x] state  - loading       -> AutomationActivityFeedProjection.Project selects AutomationHistorySection.Loading when model.Loading (web isLoading); rendered AutomationActivityFeed.cs#BuildLoading (TsSkeleton × SkeletonRowCount=5, LiveRegion announce); tests Loading_when_model_is_loading / Loading_takes_precedence_over_present_history / Skeleton_row_count_matches_the_web_five
[x] state  - empty         -> AutomationHistorySection.Empty (web items.length === 0 → EmptyState); rendered BuildEmpty (TsEmptyState IconGlyph=ActivityGlyph, Message=EmptyMessage); tests Empty_when_resolved_without_history / Empty_message_uses_the_automations_catalog_key / Empty_automation_name_carries_the_empty_message
[x] state  - success       -> AutomationHistorySection.Populated (web items.length > 0 → HistoryRow list); rendered BuildHistoryRows → BuildHistoryRow (status glyph/accent, inline error, timeAgo, formatDurationMs, actions ratio); tests Populated_when_resolved_with_history / History_* (status map, error, ratio, time tiers, duration)

# Strings (7) — every visible literal resolves from Strings/*.resw via ILocalizer with the web key names (en/ar/he 7/7/7)
[x] string - automations.avgDuration   -> AutomationActivityFeedProjection.BuildStats localizer.GetString("translation.automations.avgDuration", "avg") (web `{formatDurationMs(avg_duration_ms)} {t('avgDuration','avg')}`)
[x] string - automations.live          -> AutomationActivityFeedProjection.Project localizer.GetString("translation.automations.live", "Live") (web connected chip)
[x] string - automations.noHistory     -> AutomationActivityFeedProjection.Project localizer.GetString("translation.automations.noHistory", "No execution history yet") (web EmptyState message)
[x] string - automations.recentActivity-> AutomationActivityFeedProjection.Project localizer.GetString("translation.automations.recentActivity", "Recent Activity") (web header <h2>)
[x] string - automations.reconnecting  -> AutomationActivityFeedProjection.Project localizer.GetString("translation.automations.reconnecting", "Reconnecting") (web reconnecting chip)
[x] string - automations.successRate   -> AutomationActivityFeedProjection.BuildStats localizer.GetString("translation.automations.successRate", "success") (web `{fmtPercent(success_rate,0)} {t('successRate','success')}`)
[x] string - automations.totalRuns     -> AutomationActivityFeedProjection.BuildStats localizer.GetString("translation.automations.totalRuns", "total") (web `{total_executions} {t('totalRuns','total')}`)

